Not all friction is bad. Some of what Maya feels — exertion, uncertainty, the effort of getting a sound right — is simply what learning looks like. That's not a design failure.

What Forvo can control is whether the interface compounds that friction or absorbs it. Grounded in principles like [**Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics**](https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/), the app can feel genuinely empathetic — clear when things are hard, forgiving when things go wrong, and transparent enough that Maya always knows where she stands.

That's the foundation step 3 builds on.
